---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import { siteContent } from "../data/site";
import "../styles/legal.css";

const { companyName, logo, nav, cta, contactInfo, businessInfo } = siteContent;
const phoneHref = `tel:${contactInfo.phone.replace(/[^0-9+]/g, "")}`;
---

<MainLayout
  title="Cookie & Browser Storage Policy | Velixon"
  description="Learn how velixon.net uses essential browser storage, session attribution, and consent-based analytics and conversion measurement."
>
  <Navbar companyName={companyName} logo={logo} nav={nav} cta={cta} currentPath="/cookies" />
  <main id="main-content" class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-hero">
      <div class="container legal-hero-inner">
        <p class="legal-eyebrow">Trust center · Cookies &amp; storage</p>
        <h1>Storage should have a clear purpose.</h1>
        <p class="legal-lede">This policy explains the cookies and browser storage velixon.net may use, what each category does, and how you can control optional analytics.</p>
        <p class="legal-meta">
          <span><strong>Effective:</strong> <time datetime="2026-08-11">August 11, 2026</time></span>
          <span><strong>Applies to:</strong> velixon.net</span>
        </p>

        <div class="legal-summary" aria-label="Cookie and storage policy summary">
          <div class="legal-summary-item"><span class="legal-summary-number">01 · OPERATIONAL</span><p>First-party storage supports attribution, audit progress, quiz progress, and checklists.</p></div>
          <div class="legal-summary-item"><span class="legal-summary-number">02 · OPTIONAL</span><p>Google analytics and conversion measurement load only when configured and allowed.</p></div>
          <div class="legal-summary-item"><span class="legal-summary-number">03 · YOUR CONTROL</span><p>You can revisit analytics preferences or clear site data in your browser.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="container legal-content legal-layout">
      <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Cookie and storage policy contents">
        <p class="legal-toc-title">On this page</p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#meaning">What these terms mean</a></li>
          <li><a href="#operational">Operational storage</a></li>
          <li><a href="#analytics">Optional analytics</a></li>
          <li><a href="#providers">Provider operations</a></li>
          <li><a href="#controls">Your controls</a></li>
          <li><a href="#updates">Updates and contact</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <article class="legal-article" aria-label="Velixon Cookie and Browser Storage Policy">
        <section class="legal-section" id="meaning">
          <p class="legal-section-label">01 · Basics</p>
          <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
          <p>Cookies are small values a website or provider can store through your browser. Local storage can remain after a browser tab closes. Session storage normally lasts only for the current tab. This site uses these tools for specific operational purposes and, when available and approved by you, optional measurement.</p>
          <p>The site remains usable when optional analytics is declined. Disabling all browser storage may reset preferences or interrupt audit progress, quiz handoff, or saved checklist progress.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="operational">
          <p class="legal-section-label">02 · Operational storage</p>
          <h2>First-party storage used by the experience</h2>
          <p>Velixon may use first-party browser storage for the following purposes:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Remember that you completed or skipped the opening experience for the current visit.</li>
            <li>Preserve first-touch campaign, landing-page, and referral information during a session so an inquiry can include its source.</li>
            <li>Temporarily preserve unfinished Free Business Systems Audit field values and a random submission identifier in the current tab for up to 24 hours so the intake can be resumed and accidental duplicate submissions can be recognized. The saved draft is removed after a successful submission.</li>
            <li>Temporarily preserve Automation Maturity Quiz progress and its browser-local result separately from the audit request.</li>
            <li>Save interactive checklist progress on the current device until you reset the checklist or clear site data.</li>
            <li>Prevent a successful submission message from being shown repeatedly after navigation.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>This operational storage is separate from Google Analytics. It is used to provide the requested workflow, maintain continuity, or record the source of an inquiry—not for cross-site advertising.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="analytics">
          <p class="legal-section-label">03 · Optional analytics</p>
          <h2>Analytics loads only after permission</h2>
          <p>If Velixon configures a verified Google Analytics property, Google Ads conversion destination, Google Tag Manager container, or Microsoft Clarity project, the applicable library loads only after you select <strong>Allow analytics</strong>. Those services may then use cookies or similar browser technologies to distinguish visits, measure how the website is used, and record a completed inquiry as a conversion.</p>
          <p>Advertising storage, advertising user-data storage, and ad-personalization storage remain denied. Velixon does not use the website's consent choice to enable advertising cookies.</p>
          <p>If optional measurement is configured, local storage remembers whether your choice is granted or denied so the website can respect it on later visits. When measurement is not configured, no analytics preference or Google measurement cookie is needed.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="providers">
          <p class="legal-section-label">04 · Providers</p>
          <h2>Hosting and service-provider operations</h2>
          <p>Netlify delivers the website, processes forms, runs the audit endpoint, stores audit requests, and provides operational security and network services. Resend may be configured to deliver audit-related email. Optional strategy calls are arranged manually after audit delivery, so this website does not load a scheduling provider. These and other infrastructure providers may process request or device information and use their own necessary technologies to operate and protect their services. Those provider operations are governed by their own policies and are distinct from optional site analytics.</p>
          <p>Submitted website inquiries and audit records are subject to the retention periods described in the <a href="/privacy/#retention">Privacy Policy</a>. Clearing browser storage removes browser-local data but does not delete a form or audit request already submitted to Velixon.</p>
          <p>Learn more in the <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/">Netlify Privacy Statement</a>, <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy">Resend Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>, and <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="controls">
          <p class="legal-section-label">05 · Controls</p>
          <h2>Change or remove stored information</h2>
          <p>When optional analytics is configured, use <strong>Analytics preferences</strong> in the footer to allow, decline, or revisit analytics. Withdrawing permission applies to future analytics activity and does not automatically erase data already processed by a provider.</p>
          <p>You can also use your browser settings to block cookies, remove site data, or clear local and session storage. Those controls vary by browser. Clearing storage may reset your analytics choice, intro preference, attribution, unfinished audit or quiz, or saved checklist progress.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section" id="updates">
          <p class="legal-section-label">06 · Updates</p>
          <h2>Policy updates and questions</h2>
          <p>Browser technologies and provider behavior can change. Velixon may update this page when the website's storage practices or services change. The effective date above identifies the current version.</p>
        </section>

        <aside class="legal-contact" aria-labelledby="cookie-contact-title">
          <h2 id="cookie-contact-title">Questions about cookies or storage?</h2>
          <p>Contact Velixon if you want help understanding the website's storage practices or exercising a privacy choice.</p>
          <p><strong>{businessInfo.legalName}</strong>, doing business as {businessInfo.doingBusinessAs}<br />Mailing address: {businessInfo.mailingAddress.formatted}</p>
          <div class="legal-contact-links">
            <a href={`mailto:${contactInfo.email}?subject=Cookie%20and%20Storage%20Question`}>{contactInfo.email}</a>
            <a href={phoneHref}>{contactInfo.phone}</a>
            <a href="/contact/">Contact form</a>
          </div>
          <div class="legal-related"><strong>Related:</strong> <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a><a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a><a href="/security/">Security</a><a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility</a></div>
        </aside>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</MainLayout>
